11. Service Water-Heating Systems (continued)
3. Service water heating use can be demonstrated to be reduced
by reducing the hot fraction of mixed water to achieve
required operational temperature. Examples include shower
or laundry heat recovery to incoming cold-water supply,
reducing the hot-water fraction required to meet required
mixed-water temperature. Such reduction shall be demon-
strated by calculations.
h. Gas storage water heaters shall be modeled using natural gas as
their fuel.
Exception: Where natural gas is not available for the proposed
site, as determined by the rating authority, gas storage water
heaters shall be modeled using propane as their fuel.
i. Piping losses shall not be modeled.
