c. Water Main Temperatures for Service Water-Heating Calcu-
lations. It is acceptable to use either an annual water main supply
temperature or monthly average water main supply temperatures
for calculating service water heating. If annual or monthly water
main supply temperatures are not available from the local water
utility, annual average ground temperatures may be used.
15. Distribution Transformers
Low-voltage dry-type distribution transformers shall be modeled if the Low-voltage dry-type distribution transformers shall be modeled only if
transformers in the proposed design exceed the efficiency required in the proposed design transformers exceed the efficiency requirements of
Table 8.4.4. Table 8.4.4. A transformer with a kVA rating not listed in the table shall
have its minimum efficiency level calculated by a linear interpolation of
the kVA and efficiency values listed in the table immediately above and
below its kVA rating. If modeled, the efficiency requirements from Table
8.4.4 or the interpolated efficiency requirements shall be used. The ratio
of the capacity to peak electrical load of the transformer shall be the
same as the ratio in the proposed design.
